# Migrate Solution Pages to Rich Text (Portable Text)

This plan outlines the steps to correctly upload the perfectly generated MDX files into Sanity so that they appear in the clean, section-by-section Rich Text editor (`structuredSections`), preserving all formatting, paragraphs, and tables.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Because you have generated extremely rich MDX files (up to 3,700 words), we are **abandoning the JSON prompt to Codex**. Do not ask Codex for JSON. We will use your existing MDX files exactly as they are.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Update Sanity Schema

We will upgrade the **Solution Page** schema so it gets the exact same editing experience as Module pages.

#### [MODIFY] [solutionPageType.ts](file:///c:/Users/nikhi/OneDrive/Documents/classgrid_marketting/sanity/schemaTypes/solutionPageType.ts)
- Replace the basic `markdownSections` text-field array with the `structuredSections` array.
- This uses Sanity's `richBody` (Portable Text), which supports headings, paragraphs, lists, bold text, and the custom `richTable` layout.

### 2. Custom Migration Script

We will write a robust Node script (`scripts/upload-to-portable-text.mjs`) that:
- Reads your 8 existing `.mdx` files.
- Identifies every section (`## Heading`).
- Parses every paragraph, converting `**bold**` into Sanity's `strong` marks.
- Parses every bullet point into Sanity's `listItem: "bullet"` blocks.
- Parses every `<table>` into Sanity's native `richTable` format.
- Uploads the fully formed JSON directly into `structuredSections` in Sanity.

## Verification Plan
1. Run the script locally across all 8 pages.
2. Open Sanity Studio and verify that `for-admins` shows separate, editable Rich Text sections.
3. Verify that paragraphs are intact (not merged into one heavy block).
4. Verify that the tables render inside the Sanity Rich Text editor and the frontend.
